# Conformance probe pack for the mapping rules of spec 0.6 on the `xml` wire.
# Public. Every kind has its own `root`, so the pack has none. Exercises a root
# per kind, `const` and `default` in common and in a kind, a `when` and a
# `field` on one locator (ruling 26 of 0.5) and `when ... present` on a scalar
# no field maps (ruling 27 of 0.5).
format  conformance-rules-xml
version 0.6.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
wire    xml
field   uid       @id          string
const   @v        1
default callsign  NONE
kind     track
root     trk
requires lat lon
field    lat       pos/@lat     float
field    lon       pos/@lon     float
field    callsign  name/#text   string
const    pos/@datum  WGS84
kind     tagged                 # `mode` holds the `when` value, at the place of the `field` line
root     note
requires how
field    how       @mode        string
field    callsign  @name        string
when     @mode     fixed
kind     marked                 # `mark` is not mapped by the `when`: it is residue
root     note
requires ce
when     @mark     present
field    ce        @ce          float
kind     plain
root     item
